+// item (medkits, food, drugs) reach the server as intents (kinds 9 and 10);
+// the server validates them on its own state and the engine applies them to
+// the player's actor on the server (CInventory::Slot/Belt/Ruck, the installed
+// `CInventory__eat` check and CInventory::Eat inside the player's script
+// context). An equip is committed before it is applied (it is deterministic);
+// a use is applied first, because only the engine and the installed scripts
+// know what it does, then its resolved post-state is committed before the
+// player is answered: a termination in between loses an unacknowledged use
+// with everything it did (the checkpoint's state comes back whole). Both
+// records are absolute post-state, so a replay is idempotent.
+//
+// Clients learn each participant actor's inventory layout (every item's
+// place, slot and remaining uses) from CampaignEvent 9, sent whenever the
+// server's layout changes and when a client enters the world.
+
+const u8 kPlaceSlot = 1, kPlaceBelt = 2, kPlaceRuck = 3;
